{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeqTLTc4gyY58cmXnzHo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rejected attempt was a copy of the live model `heads_default_alternation_ideal`, so I switched to a different mechanism. The new candidate passes the self-check, which prints `OK`. Novelty against the other models still has to be checked at admission, and the self-check doesn't cover that.\n\n**Model name:** `streak_excess_person_sensitivity_ideal`\n\n**Hypothesis:** I refined the incumbent, `person_sensitivity_length_scaled_ideal`, and kept its mechanism as it is:\n- each person has their own ideal switching rate;\n- each person has their own sensitivity, which scales with the number of transitions;\n- everyone shares a penalty for visibly periodic sequences.\n\nThe one change is a shared penalty for long streaks. Every flip beyond two in a sequence's longest run (HHH, HHHH, ...) makes it look less random. This targets the critique finding that survived the FDR correction: among pairs with the same switch count, people pick the sequence with the shorter longest run more often than the incumbent predicts (observed 0.588 vs 0.444, q = 0.048).\n\n**Why it should pass novelty:** No live model adds a streak penalty to the incumbent. The closest ones add streak penalties to weaker models: `personal_lapse_ideal_streak_excess`, `periodic_ideal_absolute_streak_penalty` and `length_scaled_alternation_ideal_streak`. If the fitted streak weight comes out near zero, though, its predictions will match the incumbent's. In that case the novelty gate could still reject it as a near-duplicate.\n\n**Self-check result:** The short smoke fit (100 draws, 1 chain) scored ELPD-LOO −1047.2, against the incumbent's −1047.1. That run is too small to say whether it beats the incumbent. It also warned that PSIS-LOO looked unreliable (10.1% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5), and R-hat can't be computed from one chain. The full admission fit with more draws and chains will settle both.\n\nThe three files are in `.../experiment1/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_4_repair_1/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3368,"cache_read_input_tokens":72724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3368,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"811a181c-c65e-4e66-b1e9-c8e52d911e0b","uuid":"36da6043-db28-401a-80ed-8ab7dd65ef6b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T06:32:58.322Z","request_id":"req_011CfeqTKVaSxu6bheHkc3cG"}
